# XCU mesg
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Only the case without a terminal can be run from a script, because the
# utility acts on the first terminal among the three standard streams and a
# test must not change a person's terminal.

assertion  XCU.mesg.001
anchor     utilities/mesg.html#EXIT STATUS
anchor     utilities/mesg.html#DESCRIPTION
class      disputed
says       When none of standard input, output and error is a terminal, mesg
           with no operand reports an error with an exit status above one.
note       disputed (standard issue candidate, not yet numbered): the page
           says the terminal is the first one among the three standard
           streams and gives status above 1 for "an error", but never says
           that having no such terminal is an error; a FAIL is logged as
           INSPECT. Only the form without an operand is run, so that nothing
           can be changed even where a system looks further for a terminal.
test       t/001-no-terminal.sh

assertion  XCU.mesg.002
anchor     utilities/mesg.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/mesg.html#STDOUT
anchor     utilities/mesg.html#EXIT STATUS
class      untestable
says       mesg y and mesg n grant and deny messages to the terminal, and mesg
           alone reports the state and exits zero when messages are allowed
           and one when they are not.
reason     It needs a terminal device that the test may change, and a script run
           by the driver has none.
